  "name": "flight",
  "vibe": "A departure film. A daylight sky graded from a pale horizon to a deeper zenith, a warm sun disc bleeding light, drifting cloud banks and a dark ground plane with a dashed runway centreline that scrolls beneath you. One hot orange against all that blue. A simple aircraft mark crosses the frame on every beat — taxiing on the opener, banking up and away on the reveal — and EVERY PICTURE RIDES A DEVICE: a browser card with three traffic lights and the site address in a mono url pill, or a handset with an ink bezel and a notch. The cruise beat lays five of them across the frame in a deliberately unequal mosaic; the instruments beat sets a sweeping gauge beside the readouts. Authored landscape-first (16:9) as a native GSAP + DOM composition, sharing one module with its 9:16 cut. Best for travel, logistics, mobility, onboarding and any brand whose story is going somewhere.",
